    "created_at": "2022-09-12T20:35:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-12T20:35:23Z",
    "body": "> Incidentally, I note that the second argument, which is a spec-internal enum value \"key\", is marked up as if it were a variable name. That seems potentially confusing. Is there better markup which could be used here? Ecma262 uses a monospace font for enum values.\r\n\r\nThat looks like just a bug; thanks for catching! I think so far we've been using no distinguished font for Ecma enums? Please feel free to just remove the `<var>` in that case.",
